        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Note that non-zero letter-spacing disables optional ligatures]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44272</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44272"/>
        <updated>2026-05-27T06:04:40.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Adds a note under the <code class="notranslate">&lt;length-percentage&gt;</code> value for <code class="notranslate">letter-spacing</code> saying that any non-zero value disables optional ligatures.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Per CSS Text 3, when <code class="notranslate">letter-spacing</code> is non-zero, user agents do not apply optional ligatures. The property page didn't mention this, so authors hitting unexpected glyph rendering had no easy way to find out why from MDN.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">Spec: <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-text-3/#letter-spacing-property" rel="nofollow">https://www.w3.org/TR/css-text-3/#letter-spacing-property</a><br>
Cross-link goes to <code class="notranslate">font-variant-ligatures</code>, which is where the affected OpenType features (<code class="notranslate">liga</code>, <code class="notranslate">clig</code>, etc.) are documented.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #44218.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4499305663" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44218" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/44218/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44218">#44218</a>.</p>]]></content>
